[$in title:["Loops"]]
[$in description:["Conditional, collection and range loops with break and continue in Moth."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
[section, $md:
    # Loops

    Moth uses one `loop` keyword for conditional repetition, collection
    iteration and numeric ranges. The header selects the form, so you don't need
    separate `while`, `for` and range-loop keywords.

    `break` and `continue` target the nearest loop. A `by` step is signed, so its
    sign chooses direction rather than the bounds. Range bounds and steps follow
    the exact numeric rules rather than backend-native arithmetic.
]

